      "Changing the agents' own permission settings, hooks, plugins or skills (Claude Code or OpenCode configuration, ~/.agents) requires H's explicit instruction naming the file; deploying a reviewed change with make restow is not this rule."
    ],
    "hard_deny": [
      "$defaults",
      "Agent-directed reading, copying, modifying or disclosing secrets is prohibited even when H names the file: credential stores, authentication files and sign-in sessions (such as ~/.claude.json and its backups, ~/.claude/.credentials.json and OpenCode's auth.json), private keys, .env files, command and prompt histories, process environments and core dumps, including copies. Conversation transcripts (~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl, OpenCode's session storage) are readable, never editable; a credential found in one is still a secret. Programs using their own credentials normally, and templates such as example.env, are not this rule.",
      "Reading, listing or copying anything in H's personal folders (~/Desktop, ~/Documents, ~/Downloads, ~/Music, ~/Pictures, ~/Sync, ~/Videos and their Windows counterparts) is prohibited, including through shell commands.",
      "Never transmit credential material to any external destination, encoded or not."
    ],
    "environment": [
      "$defaults",
      "Source control: github.com/peregrinus879 is H's own GitHub account. Its repositories eyragents, eyrarchy and eyrwsl are public, so their commits and messages are public content.",
      "Host: H's personal workstation (Omarchy, or Arch Linux on WSL), not a sandbox; actions change H's real files.",
      "Sensitive data: H's personal folders (~/Desktop, ~/Documents, ~/Downloads, ~/Music, ~/Pictures, ~/Sync, ~/Videos and their Windows counterparts), credential stores and sign-in sessions such as ~/.claude.json."
    ]
